Here is a tip calculator as a single HTML page: type the bill and the tip percentage, and it shows the tip and the total.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Tip calculator</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 22rem; margin: 2rem auto; }
    label, input, output { display: block; margin: 0.5rem 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    input { width: 100%; padding: 0.4rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Tip calculator</h1>
  <form id="form">
    <label for="bill">Bill (EGP)</label>
    <input id="bill" inputmode="decimal" value="0">
    <input id="tip" type="number" value="10">
  </form>
  <output id="result">Tip: <span id="tip-amount">0.00</span>,
    total: <span id="total">0.00</span></output>
  <script>
    const bill = document.getElementById("bill");
    const tip = document.getElementById("tip");
    function update() {
      const amount = parseInt(bill.value);
      const share = (amount * Number(tip.value)) / 100;
      document.getElementById("tip-amount").textContent = share.toFixed(2);
      const total = amount + share;
      document.getElementById("total").textContent = total.toFixed(2);
    }
    document.getElementById("form").addEventListener("input", update);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

Save it as an .html file and open it in a browser.

You're right. `parseInt` stops at the decimal point, so 85.50 became 85 and the tip was computed on the wrong amount. `Number` keeps the decimals. I also added the missing label for the tip field.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Tip calculator</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 22rem; margin: 2rem auto; }
    label, input, output { display: block; margin: 0.5rem 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    input { width: 100%; padding: 0.4rem; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Tip calculator</h1>
  <form id="form">
    <label for="bill">Bill (EGP)</label>
    <input id="bill" inputmode="decimal" value="0">
    <label for="tip">Tip (%)</label>
    <input id="tip" type="number" value="10">
  </form>
  <output id="result">Tip: <span id="tip-amount">0.00</span>,
    total: <span id="total">0.00</span></output>
  <script>
    const bill = document.getElementById("bill");
    const tip = document.getElementById("tip");
    function update() {
      const amount = Number(bill.value);
      const share = (amount * Number(tip.value)) / 100;
      document.getElementById("tip-amount").textContent = share.toFixed(2);
      const total = amount + share;
      document.getElementById("total").textContent = total.toFixed(2);
    }
    document.getElementById("form").addEventListener("input", update);
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```
